From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0097] anv, intel/mi: a batch out of memory is not written through

On top of 0096 (src/mesa-oom1 = src/mesa-prod9 + this, build-oom1). NOT installed.

When a command buffer batch cannot grow, anv_batch_emit_dwords() records the error in the batch
(anv_batch_set_error) and returns NULL; vkEndCommandBuffer then returns it. The emit macros (anv_batch_emit,
anv_batch_emitn, mi_builder_pack, blorp_emit) skip a NULL instruction, and upstream fixed the open-coded copies
the same way (1c930a505e7 "anv: don't attempt to memcpy if allocation fails", MR 37534), but the code that writes
dwords of an emitted instruction by hand did not check, nor did the code that reads batch.relocs, which stays
NULL when the first batch BO of a command buffer cannot be allocated. Upstream main (6240b967, 2026-11-03) has all
of these unchanged; this fixes them in the style of 37534: a NULL instruction is not written, nothing else changes.

dEQP-VK.wsi.headless.swapchain.simulate_oom.* with MESA_VK_WSI_DEBUG=sw (CPU images, whose blit command
buffers are recorded at swapchain creation): SIGSEGV in mi_builder (_mi_copy_no_unref from
cmd_buffer_emit_bt_pool_base_address in vkBeginCommandBuffer) and, once that was fixed, in blorp_exec
(anv_cmd_buffer_add_reloc_bo reading the NULL batch.relocs). Same on the installed prod8.

intel/common/mi_builder.h:
- mi_builder_flush_math: drop the math instead of copying it to NULL;
- _mi_copy_no_unref: immediate -> REG64 / MEM64 writes the operand dwords only if emitted;
- mi_store_relocated_imm: no token pointers into a failed instruction; mi_relocate_store_imm ignores them;
- mi_resolve_relocated_address_token: skips the store whose instruction was not emitted;
- mi_goto_if: a jump that could not be emitted is not memset nor recorded for mi_goto_target to patch.
anv:
- anv_cmd_buffer_ensure_batch_relocs(): the lazy first batch BO; anv_cmd_buffer_add_reloc_bo returns its error
  instead of using a NULL batch.relocs; same for the shader / indirect set reloc appends (bind_shaders,
  cmd_buffer_flush_gfx_state, DGC);
- open-coded dword writes after anv_batch_emitn/emit_dwords: 3DSTATE_CONSTANT_ALL, 3DSTATE_VERTEX_BUFFERS,
  3DMESH_3D, the anv_batch_emit_gfx copy in genX_cmd_draw.c (the copy of what 37534 fixed in genX_gfx_state.c),
  clear color MI_STORE_DATA_IMM, TR-TT entry writes, SO memcpy, the dummy-draw WA, simple shader, the perf query
  relocated address patching (khr_perf_query_resolve_reloc keeps begin/end paired), DGC return address, the
  secondary return address, video encode (H.264/H.265/AV1 PAK insert objects, VDENC state);
- anv_trtt_first_bind_init_queue does not submit a batch in error (as anv_sparse_bind_trtt already checks);
- vkEndCommandBuffer returns the batch status after its own emissions (it returned VK_SUCCESS even when the
  closing MI_BATCH_BUFFER_START/END or flushes could not be emitted);
- vkCmdExecuteCommands with a secondary in error (its vkEndCommandBuffer failed; CTS conditional_rendering
  ignores that result) fails the container with that error instead of executing it: exec_mode was never set
  and anv_cmd_buffer_add_secondary jumped through its switch with mode 0 (upstream only asserts);
- anv_queue_submit refuses a command buffer in error (same CTS pattern for primaries: its unterminated batch
  was chained, NULL deref in anv_cmd_buffer_chain_command_buffers; on hardware it would run an unterminated
  batch) and returns the recording error.

Tested on the build Mac (x86_64 deqp-vk under Rosetta, xemac fake device; report
docs/reports/b580-anv-oom-batch-20261104.md): wsi.headless *simulate_oom* with MESA_VK_WSI_DEBUG=sw 10 Crash ->
14/14 Pass; api.* (267509) and wsi.headless.* (4028) identical to prod9 case by case on the default path (apart
from present_id_wait.wait.* timing flakes, same in both). With a test-only injection failing ~1/50 command buffer
emissions over 11248 cases from 17 groups, prod9 crashed in 976 cases and this patch in none (1/1000: >=77 vs 0).

Generated-by: LLM

